--- !u!114 &1266104172
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1266104171}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a35e5e5e0a89b36efab07504f2c03b44, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EndingManager
  goodEndingThreshold: 70
  menuSceneName: Nour_work/Scenes/Scene_MainMenu
  continueKey: 32
  subtitleText: {fileID: 599559877}
  continueIcon: {fileID: 308722799}
  subtitlePanel: {fileID: 877320608}
  typingSpeed: 0.05
  goodLines:
  - Ah, You also saw the Waswas (Whispers)
  - Do you know why the thiefs came to your door?
  - 'Because a thief does not rob an empty house. '
  - They attacked you because you carried a treasure inside. The struggle you felt?
    That was the sign of your faith, not your failure.
  - They attacked you because you carried a treasure inside. The struggle you felt?
    That was the sign of your faith, not your failure.
  - ' I want to give you one last piece of advice for the road ahead.'
  - In the next path, your greatest enemy will not be a monster. It will be this...(He
    points to his own tongue).
  - "The tongue is the ladle of the heart. Whatever is in your heart\u2014sweet or
    sour\u2014the tongue will scoop it out and pour it into the world. "
  - If you let the Waswas poison your heart, your tongue will speak poison. And remember...
    People are toppled into the Fire by nothing but the harvest of their tongues.
  - 'Before you speak, ask yourself: Is this my voice? Or is it the Whisperer?'
  - You saved an old man today because you listened to the truth.
  - Keep listening. The noise of the world is loud... but the voice of God is constant.
    Go now. Your light is bright enough to guide others.
  - Fi Aman Allah (In the safety of God)
  - (You feel a strange lightness in your chest. The shadows in the corners seem
    to retreat.)
  badLines:
  - 'We meet again. I am sad to tell you that the candle has burnt out.

    Do not
    weep for the wick that is consumed, my son. Weep for the light that was never
    lit.'
  - 'Did you think you had time? O Son of Adam, you are nothing but a number of days.
    Whenever each day passes, then a part of you has gone.

    You thought you were
    ''killing time'' in this maze? No... time was killing you.'
  - You thought you were 'killing time' in this maze? No... time was killing you.
  - 'Do you think you wronged the people are around you? your neighbours?

'
  - No. God does not wrong the people at all, but it is the people who are wronging
    themselves. But you... you are left with the scars on your own heart.
  - No. God does not wrong the people at all, but it is the people who are wronging
    themselves. But you... you are left with the scars on your own heart.
  - Every sin, every act of neglect... it is not a mark on the world. It is a black
    spot on your own heart.
  - 'You built this maze, brick by brick, with every moment you wasted.

    Now
    you must walk the path you paved.'
  - 'The harvest is here. And you have planted only thorns.

    May Allah have mercy
    on the living... for the dead have already found their truth.'
